WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:10.800
[Your Tuberculosis Association presents]

00:00:11.219 --> 00:00:16.800
["You Can Help"]

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:23.800
[Narrator:] One of the dread four horsemen
of the apocalypse is pestilence, the plagues

00:00:24.099 --> 00:00:30.829
that have scourged mankind since earliest
times. Of these, none has claimed more lives

00:00:30.829 --> 00:00:34.530
than the white plague, tuberculosis.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:39.739
Some of the greatest names in medicine have
waged the war against TB since Hippocrates

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:46.739
first defined its symptoms five hundred years
before the time of Christ.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:52.890
But it was a little more than a hundred years
ago that the chance observation of children

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:58.489
listening to the magnified sounds of tapping
on a hollow log gave Laennec, a young French

00:00:58.489 --> 00:01:02.530
doctor, the inspiration for the stethoscope.

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:08.720
Later in the 19th century, Villemin proved
that TB was a contagious disease. Then Louis

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:13.710
Pasteur discovered that germs were the cause
of contagious disease.

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:20.550
The German scientist Koch was the first to
find the TB germ, the tubercule bacillus.

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:26.390
But not until Roentgen discovered x-ray could
the actual destruction caused by the germ

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:29.710
be seen inside the living body.

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:35.130
Modern sanatorium treatment in this country
began in the Adirondacks, when Trudeau found

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:40.740
that rest, fresh air and good food helped
him to recover from the supposedly incurable

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:41.860
TB.

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:48.610
Nineteen-hundred, and with the new century
came a new idea; to fight TB with knowledge.

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:53.890
To teach people about TB so that it can be
found early when chances for recovery are

00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:54.750
best.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:02:00.450
With this in mind, a group of scientists,
physicians, and other public-spirited citizens

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:06.560
founded what is now the National Tuberculosis
Association.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:13.420
From these beginnings came the local TB association
in your community, formed by your neighbors

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:16.540
in the interest of better public health.

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:22.840
Here's how it works; the people elect a board
of directors, representing a cross-section

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:29.840
of the community, businessmen and housewives,
churchmen, doctors, educators, newspaper men,

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:34.420
industrialists, and legislators.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:40.560
The board employs an executive secretary;
together they plan a program for tuberculosis

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:46.030
control. The secretary needs a staff of trained
technical workers to mobilize the army of

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:51.130
volunteers so necessary for community action
against TB.

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:52.470
[Fact Finding]

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:59.470
A program begins with fact-finding. The secretary
must know how many deaths were caused by TB

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:06.510
during the past year. Are there enough doctors,
nurses, social workers, sanatorium beds, clinics,

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:09.630
and hospitals?

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:16.490
Are there special groups in the community
with a higher incidence of TB? For his information,

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:19.220
the secretary consults agencies like these.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:22.520
[Image of buildings with signs outside, "Board
of Education, Medical Society, Hospitals,

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:24.730
Health Dept., Dept. Public Welfare, Chambers
of Commerce."]

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:29.640
From them he can fill in his picture of the
community, learn its weak points, know how

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:33.310
to build a most effective program.

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:39.030
Of primary importance to such a program is
health education, carefully planned with the

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:45.069
help of other community organizations. For
education must be more than merely telling

00:03:45.069 --> 00:03:52.069
a story. It was must influence behavior, form
habits of thought and action.

00:03:52.709 --> 00:03:58.630
Additional persons must be reached through
those already educated. Finally, it must create

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:03.760
a demand for more education, for which leadership
has been developed.

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:10.069
Thus the association plans its educational
program for the use of such groups as teachers

00:04:10.069 --> 00:04:17.069
and school administrators, speakers, churchmen,
and those being trained for professional careers:

00:04:19.019 --> 00:04:23.349
doctors, nurses, and social workers.

00:04:23.349 --> 00:04:29.139
The association can reach all groups because
its board of directors is drawn from all aspects

00:04:29.139 --> 00:04:34.639
of community life. Largely an educational
job is the phase of the association's work

00:04:34.639 --> 00:04:37.599
known as Case Finding.

00:04:37.599 --> 00:04:43.029
Control of TB depends on finding the people
who have it before there are symptoms, before

00:04:43.029 --> 00:04:49.259
the victims themselves are aware of it. Unknown
cases are often found by the family physician

00:04:49.259 --> 00:04:54.789
in the course of physical examinations and
among young people by tuberculin testing in

00:04:54.789 --> 00:04:55.939
the schools.

00:04:55.939 --> 00:05:02.939
If people are made aware of the value of periodic
chest x-rays, the TB discovered will usually

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:09.960
be in the early stage. If, however, TB is
not looked for until the patient displays symptoms

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:15.409
of the disease, the cases found are apt to
be in the far advanced state when cure is

00:05:15.409 --> 00:05:20.099
uncertain and costly.

00:05:20.099 --> 00:05:26.370
The association may be called upon to furnish
x-ray equipment, x-ray film, or technical

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:32.509
and clerical services until such time as the
health department can take over the responsibilities.

00:05:32.509 --> 00:05:39.509
Since TB control depends on finding unknown
and unsuspected cases; a program to wipe out

00:05:40.169 --> 00:05:45.479
the disease must strive to x-ray every adult
in the community.

00:05:45.479 --> 00:05:51.999
To do this, the health department and the
tuberculosis association organize local committees

00:05:51.999 --> 00:05:57.180
made up of public-spirited volunteers. With
their help and with the impetus given the

00:05:57.180 --> 00:06:04.180
drive by industry, church, school, and welfare
groups, complete coverage of the community

00:06:04.529 --> 00:06:11.529
is assured.

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:15.349
[Treatment]

00:06:15.349 --> 00:06:20.860
Those individuals whose x-ray indicates TB
are re-examined by the private physician and

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:26.580
the health department. The local association
may help by supplying public health nursing,

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:31.930
social service, or other professional aides
as demonstration to the community to show,

00:06:31.930 --> 00:06:36.719
for example, the need for adequate following
up of a case.

00:06:36.719 --> 00:06:42.430
Follow-up work includes the medical examination
and x-ray of contacts, the family, and close

00:06:42.430 --> 00:06:46.319
associates of the person found to have TB.

00:06:46.319 --> 00:06:51.240
When the person with TB is receiving treatment,
the association works with the sanatorium

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:57.639
staff to give him and his family the facts
they need to know about TB. The patient must

00:06:57.639 --> 00:07:02.979
be prepared for instance, for a long period
of bed treatment; perhaps training for a new

00:07:02.979 --> 00:07:05.619
job will be necessary.

00:07:05.619 --> 00:07:11.439
For early in his sanatorium stay, the association
and other agencies are beginning to plan for

00:07:11.439 --> 00:07:18.119
his eventual convalescence and re-employment.
Once discharged from the sanatorium, he can

00:07:18.119 --> 00:07:23.710
look to his family physician as well as his
TB association and health department for advice

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:29.529
on his job, his recreation, and the facilities
available for physical checkups.

00:07:29.529 --> 00:07:36.080
If the facilities for helping discharged patients
and their families do not exist, the association

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:41.419
must try to influence the proper agencies
to appropriate funds to cover the needs.

00:07:41.419 --> 00:07:42.460
[Public Information]

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:47.309
Among the greatest influencing factors open
to the TB association are the channels of

00:07:47.309 --> 00:07:54.309
public information: the press, from the large
dailies to the hand-printed school newspapers,

00:07:54.460 --> 00:08:03.300
Radio and television. A year-round public
information campaign, invaluable as an aid

00:08:03.409 --> 00:08:10.409
to an educational program, also serves to
tell you how your money is being spent, what

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:13.839
is being done for the public health in your
community.

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:21.440
[Seal Sale] The entire program of the tuberculosis association is financed by the sale of Christmas Seals

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:29.210
primarily through the mail or by volunteers selling TB seals and health bonds.

00:08:29.210 --> 00:08:34.940
Of the money collected in the community, 95
percent remains in the community and state

00:08:34.940 --> 00:08:40.860
where it was raised, thus the people who contributed
can see the visible results of service within

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:43.419
their community.

00:08:43.419 --> 00:08:49.529
The remaining five percent goes to the National
Association, which, like the state association,

00:08:49.529 --> 00:08:55.440
exists as a service organization for the local,
channeling information, producing materials,

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:57.709
and giving consultation.

00:08:57.709 --> 00:09:04.709
These three -- the national, state, and local
associations -- work together to further TB

00:09:05.019 --> 00:09:10.170
control on their respective levels. In some
instances, they can extend their work to other

00:09:10.170 --> 00:09:12.089
health needs.

00:09:12.089 --> 00:09:18.680
They also work together in the large program
of research, from which it is hoped will eventually

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:25.960
come the cure for the disease. Meanwhile,
tuberculosis, once the cause of more deaths

00:09:26.110 --> 00:09:31.990
than any other single disease, is being defeated
in the United States with the weapons now

00:09:31.990 --> 00:09:33.550
available.

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:40.550
The goal of your tuberculosis association
is to stamp out TB forever in your community.

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:44.700
You can help.

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:47.580
[ Music ]

00:09:47.589 --> 00:09:54.589
[The End, Produced for the National Tuberculosis
Association by the Paul J. Fennell Co.]

